<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Xiong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">274–334</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Xiong was the founding emperor of Cheng Han, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-kingdoms">Sixteen Kingdoms</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a>. Son of the refugee leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-te">Li Te</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a> in 304 and proclaimed himself emperor of Cheng in 306. He ruled until 334 with light taxes and simple laws, giving Sichuan a period of peace while northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> was at war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/li-xiong.jpg" alt="Li Xiong" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see below · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harvard_drs_49802792_%E7%B9%A1%E5%83%8F%E4%B8%89%E5%9C%8B%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E7%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8_v.1_(%E8%9C%80%E4%B8%BB%E6%9D%8E%E9%9B%84).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
